<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 37 — Spring Security 7.
    ordersvc/    order-service as an OAuth 2 resource server: URL rules by scope and role, deny by default,
                 Keycloak and Spring Authorization Server claims mapped to authorities, method security with
                 object-level checks
    authserver/  a development authorization server on Spring Security 7's built-in OAuth 2.1 Authorization
                 Server, configured by properties; access tokens shaped for the resource servers
    keycloak/    FoodFleet's Keycloak realm (roles, clients, audience mappers) and a compose file
  verify/run.sh measures Spring Security's password encoders compiled from the 7.1.1 sources and checks every
  Spring API this module uses against those sources.
-->
